      "writtenOn": "2019-07-18T20:39:11Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I do have long-term plans for unit-testing that I\u0027ll be sharing in the coming weeks.\n\nBasically, set up a lab of ST Nucleo boards (or other easy-to-get dev boards). Certain subsets of functionality is relatively easy to test in this manner (read/writing/erasing flash is a good candidate).\n\nShort functions are also usually help with readability: https://google.github.io/styleguide/cppguide.html#Write_Short_Functions",
      "parentUuid": "a3b5a62c_c75d9d8c",
      "revId": "24323968eaed3efa8dd28fcf650780d139ae7b3b",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
