    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "32c752f7_37581c59",
        "filename": "chip/stm32/flash-f.h",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 25,
      "author": {
        "id": 1314845
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-07-12T16:29:56Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "If I move them to the .c file it requires forward declarations in the .c file (so I can keep the \"high level\" vs \"physical layer\" functions together) and many more #ifdefs since the compiler will start to complain when it can\u0027t find the flash_physical_get_rdp_level/flash_physical_set_rdp_level functions for certain boards (they aren\u0027t actually called in that case because the call site is guarded by CONFIG_FLASH_READOUT_PROTECTION_AS_PSTATE. This is fine for the compiler when it\u0027s a non-static forward declaration, but not when it becomes static).\n\nI think adding a bunch more ifdefs ends up making the code a lot harder to read. Is it ok to keep as-is so we don\u0027t have to do that?",
      "parentUuid": "4363fdbc_6f579b60",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 24,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 25,
        "endChar": 61
      },
