      "writtenOn": "2019-07-12T16:29:56Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Same rationale as the BIT() macro change, which is to make sure that constants that might be used when shifting or with bitwise operations are unsigned.\n\nhttps://rules.sonarsource.com/c/RSPEC-854\nhttps://clang.llvm.org/extra/clang-tidy/checks/hicpp-signed-bitwise.html\nhttps://www.perforce.com/resources/qac/high-integrity-c-coding-standard-expressions\n\nHere\u0027s an example where a bug was found: https://crrev.com/c/1518660\n\nWe should do a large scale change to fix this, but I tend to get lots of push back whenever trying that.",
      "parentUuid": "bacc8ce5_ae51face",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 2037,
        "startChar": 45,
        "endLine": 2037,
        "endChar": 46
